const P = {
  asks: `What the sources ask for

• Session 5 INSTRUCTOR.md (repo, Spanish, draft) — "Coding Harness (internals)". Teach the concept, use Pi as the specimen: every block is a design decision any harness has to make. 2 h 30: 60 min of project demos (Session 4's homework as the recap), ~87 min of theory, Step 0 in class (open your own session JSONL), and an extension written by directing the agent as homework for the week.
• Vault session-5.md — the same design with a 2 h skeleton and a 35-min hands-on in class. Lists what's left: the deck, a plan B for the hands-on, a timed test on a clean machine, what's on screen during the theory, which blocks run live.
• BeerJS talk "Pi, el agente que se construye solo" (vault archive, 2026-06-25, ~30 min) — a pitch for Pi: harness layers, harness examples, the coding-agent landscape, what Pi is, VS Code vs Vim, a Claude Code vs Pi table, the four packages, the extension lifecycle, the programmatic API, and three demos (a /mascot command, subagents in three commits, Pi running in the browser). The INSTRUCTOR reuses slides 3, 9, 10 and 11 and says they need redrawing for the specimen frame.`,
  departs: `What you decided that departs from them

• Session 6 already ran, with Ale, before this session (date conflicts).
• This is the course's last class. It combines Session 5 with Session 6's open-weight models block (Diego's deck, PRs #20 and #21).`,
  stale: `Also stale against the course as it ran (facts, no decision needed beyond rewriting)

• Subagents: the INSTRUCTOR says pi-subagents is installed in Session 2 and Session 4 opens subagents through documentation. Since PR #16, Session 3 teaches the primitive and installs pi-subagents, and Session 4 showed them in its live run.
• Subagent demo size: the INSTRUCTOR says ~200 lines, the talk says ~100. Verified: the talk's demo file (04_Archive/pi-talk/demos/demo-2-subagents) has 197 lines; a later copy in 04_Archive/Projects/pi-talk has 280.
• The INSTRUCTOR's Session 6 bridge ("no handoff, the homework isn't reviewed there") describes a Session 6 that came after this one.`,
};
const Q = [
  ['q-length', `❓ How long is the last class, and what pays for the open-weight block?

The INSTRUCTOR plans 2 h 30 (60 min demos + 87 min theory, 3 min of slack). The vault note plans 2 h, and the course README says every session after the first is 2 h. Session 6 gave the open-weight block 30 min. Either version runs over once the block is added.`],
  ['q-demos', `❓ Does the 60-min project demo stay, and what does it ask?

It opens the class and carries Session 4's recap: "when did a doc help, when did it go stale". Session 4 dropped its homework on 2026-11-02 and ran as a live run, so that recap has nothing to ask about.`],
  ['q-closing', `❓ Where does the course closing happen?

The INSTRUCTOR says "el cierre del curso es de la Sesión 6, así que acá no hay despedida" and ends naming "la semana que viene se cambia el modelo". The repo's CLAUDE.md puts the 15-min open retrospective in Session 6. Session 6 already ran. Did the retrospective happen there, or does it come to this class?`],
  ['q-homework', `❓ What happens to the extension exercise?

It is homework "for the week": keep it alive, note what you fixed, try it against the new model in Session 6. No class follows this one. Options in the sources: homework (INSTRUCTOR), a 35-min hands-on in class (vault note), or Step 0 only.`],
  ['q-order', `❓ Which goes first: the harness internals or the open-weight models?

The course's arc ran "harness today, the model next week" (Session 1's LLM + tool + harness, swap the L last). The students already swapped the model in Session 6. Diego's deck ends on a Qwen adapted to Pi, a model trained for one harness.`],
  ['q-mcp', `❓ How does MCP appear now that Pi 1 ships it?

The talk says Pi has no MCP ("extensions cover the same ground"), and the INSTRUCTOR leaves out "MCP as one more extension" (adapter + proxy tool). Its own pendientes say Pi 1 ships MCP built in with exposure (codemode, deferred, direct), and Session 3 already taught that. Diego's propuesta-mcp/ deck (MCP transports, code mode inside, FastMCP) is waiting on a decision.`],
  ['q-pitch', `❓ Which of the talk's slides come over, and how?

The talk sells Pi: VS Code vs Vim, the Claude Code vs Pi table, "you just built what Claude Code ships as a feature". The INSTRUCTOR says "no comparison and no table" and names the risk of a Pi feature tour. The talk's table is also dated (Pi ✗ MCP).`],
];
self.P = P; self.Q = Q;
