 ['t-demos', `Demos (code in the vault archive)
• Demo 1 — /mascot: one registerCommand, an ASCII goat. Only the PROMPT.md is archived.
• Demo 2 — subagents in three commits: a foreground delegate tool → background subagents whose result comes back as a followUp → a pipeline (research → implement → review). Verified: subagents.ts has 197 lines (pi-talk/demos) and 280 (Projects/pi-talk/demos).
• Demo 3 — Pi in the browser: pi-ai + pi-agent-core bundled client-side, a virtual filesystem replacing read/write/edit, chat on the left, live preview on the right (Vite app in demos/demo-3-browser-agent, with PLAN.md).`],
 ['t-format', `Format: ~31 min, mixed audience, a pitch that ends on "install it". Slides as markdown specs per slide (layout: floating windows) plus a built slides.html (349 KB). The talk's loop diagram (pi-talk.md) is a shorter version with message_end; slide 10 carries the full event list the INSTRUCTOR uses.

Asserted by the talk, dated now: Pi has no MCP; Claude Code is Anthropic-only; Claude Code subagents always block.`],
];
