const ans = `What propuesta-mcp/ is

An 11-slide animated deck Diego built for Session 3 and cut for time. It lives in sessions/session-5/propuesta-mcp/index.html. Its cover says "Propuesta para la Sesión 5 · salió de la Sesión 3 … a coordinar con Agus: no está en el plan de la Sesión 5". It has two halves.

MCP from the inside (4 slides)
• Two layers: transport (stdio or Streamable HTTP) and data (JSON-RPC 2.0, the same tools/list and tools/call messages over either).
• Code mode: with direct calls every tool result passes through the model; in code mode the model writes code that runs in a sandbox and calls the tools.
• What the model writes: the host generates a typed API from the MCP schemas, so tools are functions; filtering (deduplicating thousands of logs) happens inside the sandbox and costs no context; only console.log comes back.
• Code mode needs a sandbox: no network, only the tool stubs; the host keeps the credentials; approving the script doesn't approve each call it makes; timeout and memory limit; one server's output is untrusted input for another.

FastMCP (6 slides, Python)
• Section cover: uv add fastmcp; its high-level API went into the official Python SDK in 2024.
• A server in 20 lines: type hints become the inputSchema, the docstring the description.
• Run it: stdio for yourself, --transport http for others.
• The client: the same one to use it and to test it, in memory with no network or processes.
• Compose servers: mount (in process) and proxy (remote), with namespaces so tool names don't collide.
• Server-side transforms: BM25SearchTransform and CodeMode change what the client sees in tools/list.

Facts
• Verified: 11 slides; added in 4f46077 (Diego, 2026-10-24, the Session 3 deck commit); not in the INSTRUCTOR's plan or timing.
• The INSTRUCTOR's pendientes place it as a candidate for the three-ways block (MCP is the form for tools other people use) and the sandbox ladder.
• Asserted by the INSTRUCTOR's pendientes: Pi 1 ships MCP with exposure, codemode by default; Session 3 taught that. So the students have used code mode without seeing it from the inside.`;
